<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
  com.claude.boot-resume — P0-10 agent half (T-P16-2/-7): the post-login reboot-recovery chain.
  RunAtLoad fires it at GUI login; it detects sessions that were open at last boot (durable
  cc-registry ghosts vs kern.boottime) and either PAGES the boot-delta once (posture=page, default)
  or resumes them + starts keepalive (posture=resume). Idempotent per boot — exactly one page per
  reboot; every post-first run this boot is a cheap already-processed abstain.

  TEMPLATE — NOT auto-loaded. This ships UNLOADED on purpose: the reboot-posture decision is the
  OPERATOR's (auto-login/FileVault/LaunchDaemon tradeoff), and whether the chain RESUMES vs only
  PAGES is the posture switch (ruling #1: PAGES by default, never auto-recovers). The agent never
  loads launchd. Activation + rollback + the posture switch: docs/activation/boot-resume-activate-snippet.md.
  Kill-switch: launchctl bootout gui/$UID/com.claude.boot-resume

  StartInterval 300s is a self-heal RETRY, not a poll: if the desk role is absent at login the page
  can't deliver, so the run fails LOUD without marking the boot processed; the 5-min tick re-attempts
  until it delivers, then every further tick abstains (already-processed) until the next reboot.
  PATH prepends ~/.claude/bin so cc-notify (+ jq) resolve — launchd's default PATH lacks it.
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
    <key>Label</key>
    <string>com.claude.boot-resume</string>

    <key>ProgramArguments</key>
    <array>
        <string>/bin/bash</string>
        <string>-c</string>
        <string>export PATH="$HOME/.claude/bin:/opt/homebrew/bin:/usr/local/bin:/usr/bin:/bin"; exec /bin/bash "$HOME/.claude/scripts/boot-resume.sh"</string>
    </array>

    <key>RunAtLoad</key>
    <true/>

    <key>StartInterval</key>
    <integer>300</integer>

    <!--
      NO ProcessType KEY, DELIBERATELY (2026-09-30). `ProcessType Background` is Darwin's darwinbg
      TASK ROLE: every descendant is pinned at PRI 4 on the E-cores and nothing inside can lift it
      (the measurement is in com.claude.postland-verify.plist, which dropped the key for the same
      reason). This job runs at login, INTO the boot storm (loadavg 346 at boot+2 min), and at PRI 4
      it starves: measured 2026-09-30 at load 185, one run sat 10 minutes inside
      `sysctl -n kern.boottime` alone, and the login run took more than 17 minutes.

      NO taskpolicy CLAMP, Nice OR LowPriorityIO EITHER (2026-10-21, REPORT.md R5). The utility band
      that replaced the task role still ranked the restore below every claude process (priority 20
      against 31): the same glob took 3.4 s at default priority and 24-46 s at the job's, admission to
      launch grew from 4 s to 278 s, and the 2026-10-21 restore took 88 minutes. The restore now runs
      at normal priority; only the routine tick of an already-handled boot demotes itself, inside
      boot-resume.sh (`taskpolicy -c utility`, fail-open). The storm is bounded where the spawning
      happens: capacity admission per pane in cc-resume-layout.sh. Run by interpreter path, not by its
      #! line: a #! exec keeps 1 KiB of kernel memory per exec on 15.x.

      Logs go to ~/.claude/logs (launchd expands no $HOME here), not /tmp: a reboot erases /tmp, and
      the run worth reading is always the one just before or after a reboot.
    -->

    <key>StandardOutPath</key>
    <string>/Users/chrisren/.claude/logs/boot-resume.stdout.log</string>

    <key>StandardErrorPath</key>
    <string>/Users/chrisren/.claude/logs/boot-resume.stderr.log</string>
</dict>
</plist>
